§ `Tests of regulations 17 to 19 applied to a day and to the 156 weeks`

-- A day of the absence: the weeks of the absence as at the day. 13 weeks is the first 13 weeks; more than 13 is not.
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` `an ordinary holiday of 20 weeks` `as at` 13
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` `an ordinary holiday of 20 weeks` `as at` 1
#ASSERT NOT (`regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` `an ordinary holiday of 20 weeks` `as at` 13.5)
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` `treatment abroad for 40 weeks` `as at` 26
#ASSERT NOT (`regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` `treatment abroad for 40 weeks` `as at` 26.5)
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` `evacuated, Scottish Ministers satisfied` `as at` 26
#ASSERT NOT (`regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` `evacuated, but nobody satisfied` `as at` 14)
-- Regulation 19(1) has no time limit.
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` `serving abroad for 100 weeks` `as at` 100
-- Not temporarily absent: never.
#ASSERT NOT (`regs 17 to 19: C is treated as present on the day of this absence` `a long stay of 20 weeks, not temporary` `as at` 1)

-- The 156 weeks: the weeks of one absence that count.
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: the weeks of this absence treated as present` `an ordinary holiday of 20 weeks` EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: the weeks of this absence treated as present` `an ordinary holiday of 10 weeks` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: the weeks of this absence treated as present` `treatment abroad for 40 weeks` EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: the weeks of this absence treated as present` `serving abroad for 100 weeks` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: the weeks of this absence treated as present` `a long stay of 20 weeks, not temporary` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: the weeks of all these absences treated as present` (LIST `an ordinary holiday of 20 weeks`, `treatment abroad for 40 weeks`) EQUALS 39
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: the weeks of all these absences treated as present` (LIST `an ordinary holiday of 10 weeks`, `an ordinary holiday of 10 weeks`) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `regs 17 to 19: the weeks of all these absences treated as present` EMPTY EQUALS 0

§ `Tests of regulations 20, 20A and 21`

-- reg 20: (resident outside Great Britain as a member of the forces, living with such a person, relationship)
#ASSERT `reg 20: C is treated as habitually resident in Great Britain for the purposes of regulation 16(c)` TRUE FALSE `some other relationship`
#ASSERT `reg 20: C is treated as habitually resident in Great Britain for the purposes of regulation 16(c)` FALSE TRUE `daughter`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 20: C is treated as habitually resident in Great Britain for the purposes of regulation 16(c)` FALSE TRUE `some other relationship`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 20: C is treated as habitually resident in Great Britain for the purposes of regulation 16(c)` FALSE FALSE `spouse`)

-- reg 20A: all four conditions.
#ASSERT `reg 20A: C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 20A: C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 20A: C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 20A: C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 20A: C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- reg 21: terminally ill and claims expressly on that ground.
#ASSERT `reg 21: regulation 16 applies as if paragraph (b) were omitted` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21: regulation 16 applies as if paragraph (b) were omitted` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21: regulation 16 applies as if paragraph (b) were omitted` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21: regulation 16 applies as if paragraph (b) were omitted` FALSE FALSE)

-- The three routes to being treated as present in England and Wales for regulation 16(a).
#ASSERT `reg 16(a): C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day by one of regulations 17 to 19, 20A, 23ZB(2) and 23ZC(7)` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 16(a): C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day by one of regulations 17 to 19, 20A, 23ZB(2) and 23ZC(7)` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 16(a): C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day by one of regulations 17 to 19, 20A, 23ZB(2) and 23ZC(7)` FALSE FALSE TRUE
